    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "4f52a404bc6a344ea2395accc538ab99",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2043,
    "chunk_text": "Also, Sir, I would like omit my first question from the set of questions under this and start with the second question because I have come to understand that the matters raised in the first question had been addressed since I submitted the Question. I spoke to the Hon.\n\n1397 1398\n\n[\u0d9c\u0dad\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0dc3\u0da2\u0dd2\u0dad\u0dca \u0dba\u0dda\u0db8\u0daf\u0dcf\u0dc3 \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dca\u200d\u0dcf]\n\n2026 \u0dc3\u0dd0\u0dca \u0dad\u0dca\u200d\u0dd0\u0db8\u0dca\u0db6 11\n\n2. The Hon. Bimal Rathnayake has stated that the Government has the final say on these projects that I mentioned and the economic development projects must benefit the people. This is a matter for the Ministry of Ports and Civil Aviation. As he is not the Minister in charge of ports or civil aviation, I would like to know in what official capacity were these statements made and do they represent the Government policy?\n\nThat is a statement the Hon. Minister had made in Jaffna to say that the projects which are to be done in the North, especially the projects of the KKS Port and the Palaly Airport, will only be done if they benefit the people and that the Government of Sri Lanka will decide if they are needed or not. Therefore, I want a clarification on that.\n\n3. Given that the Palaly Airport and the KKS Port would directly benefit people in the North and the East through improved passenger and cargo connectivity, tourism, employment, trade and investment, what assessment has the Government undertaken to determine that these projects would not sufficiently benefit the people?\n\nThis Question comes up because of that statement made that those may not be beneficial to the people. The KKS Port and the Palaly Airport may not be beneficial to the people was part of the statement that was made by the said Minister, which is why I want to know if the Government has done any assessment on this.\n\n4. On what feasibility studies, passenger-demand projections, revenue forecasts or cost-benefit analyses has the comparison between the Jaffna International Airport and the Mattala Airport been made and will those be tabled before Parliament?"
  },
  {
