    "chunk_text": "\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0db8\u0dda\u0da2\u0dbb\u0dca \u0da2\u0dd9\u0db1\u0dbb\u0dcf\u0dbd\u0dca (\u0dc0\u0dd2\u0dc1\u0dca\u200d\u0dbb\u0dcf\u0dcf\u0db8\u0dd2\u0d9a) \u0d85\u0dbb\u0dd4\u0dab \u0da2\u0dba\u0dc3\u0dda\u0d9a\u0dbb \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf \u0dad\u0dcf (\u0d86\u0dbb\u0d9a\u0dca\u0dc2\u0d9a \u0db1\u0dd2\u0dba\u0ddd\u0da2\u0dca\u200d\u0dba\u0dba \u0d85\u0db8\u0dcf\u0dad\u0dca\u200d\u0dba\u0dba\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dcf)\u0dcf) (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0bae\u0bc7\u0b9c\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0b9c\u0bc6\u0ba9\u0bb0\u0bb2\u0bcd (\u0b93\u0baf\u0bcd\u0bb5\u0bc1\u0baa\u0bc6\u0bb1\u0bcd\u0bb1) \u0b85\u0bb0\u0bc1\u0ba3 \u0b9c\u0baf\u0b9a\u0bc7\u0b95\u0bb0 \u0b95\u0bb0 - \u0baa\u0bbe\u0ba4\u0bc1\u0b95\u0bbe\u0baa\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0baa\u0bcd \u0baa\u0bbf\u0bb0\u0ba4\u0bbf \u0b85\u0bae\u0bc8\u0b9a\u0bcd\u0b9a\u0bb0\u0bcd)\u0b9a\u0bcd\u0b9a\u0bb0\u0bcd) (The Hon. Major General (Rtd.) Aruna Jayasekera - Deputy Minister of Defence) \u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0d9a\u0dae\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dba\u0d9a\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0db1\u0dd2, \u0dd4\u0db8\u0db1\u0dd2, the Hon. Ravi Karunanayake had asked nine questions about the El Ni\u00f1o effect and our preparedness for it.\n\nThe Answer is as follows:\n\n1. The National El Ni\u00f1o Preparedness and Response Plan :\n\n2. Lead coordinating mechanism:\n\nUnder the Disaster Management Act, No.13 of 2005, the Disaster Management Centre functions as the national coordinating agency for disaster management. For El Ni\u00f1o-related disaster risks, the Disaster Management Centre coordinates with the already established official subcommittee lead by the Ministry of Environment for preparedness and response activities and further, with the Department of Meteorology, the NBRI, the Irrigation Department, the Mahaweli Authority,\n\n2063 2064\n\n[\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 (\u0d86\u0da0\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dba) \u0d91\u0db8\u0dca.\u0d91\u0dbd\u0dca.\u0d92.\u0d91\u0db8\u0dca. \u0dc4\u0dd2\u0dc3\u0dca\u0db6\u0dd4\u0dbd\u0dca\u0dbd\u0dcf\u0dc4\u0dca \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf] \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf]\n\n2026 \u0dc3\u0dd0\u0db4\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd0\u0db8\u0dca\u0db6\u0dbb\u0dca 24\n\nthe Water Management Secretariat, the District Secretariats, provincial administrations and other Line Ministries through national and district coordination mechanisms. Technical leadership for sector-specific interventions remains with the respective line agencies. In this regard, the Cabinet-appointed Subcommittee and the Technical Committee on the management of El Ni\u00f1o climate impacts chaired by the Hon. (Dr.) Dammika Patabendi, Minister of Environment has met four times on 30th June, 2026, 20th July, 2026, 17th August, 2026 and 31st August, 2026 respectively. At those meetings, the following matters had been discussed and decisions were taken on.\n\n\u2022 Official communication of climate updates: The Department of Meteorology should be responsible for issuing official updates and information regarding the prevailing and anticipated climatic conditions."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_hansard_2020s",
    "doc_id": "2026-09-24-2026-09-24",
    "num": "2026-09-24",
    "date_str": "2026-09-24",
    "description": "Hansard of 2026-09-24",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.parliament.lk/en/business-of-parliament/hansards",
    "lang": "si-ta-en",
    "url_pdf": "https://www.parliament.lk/uploads/businessdocs/english/24400_english_2026-09-24.pdf",
    "chunk_id": "2026-09-24-2026-09-24-0076",
    "chunk_index": 76,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "fee843eb118a12ff015756a9e9466f14",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1854,
    "chunk_text": "\u2022 Official communication of climate updates: The Department of Meteorology should be responsible for issuing official updates and information regarding the prevailing and anticipated climatic conditions.\n\n\u2022 National Action Plan and coordinated preparedness: The need to develop a National Action Plan with a clear implementation timeline to guide preparedness and response measures was emphasized. Relevant government institutions should work through a single, coordinated process to ensure effective implementation.\n\n\u2022 Sector-specific impacts: It has been recognized that the impacts of El Ni\u00f1o could vary significantly across sectors depending on the timing and duration of the climatic conditions. Agriculture has been identified as the sector most likely to be significantly affected, requiring particular attention in preparedness and response planning.\n\n\u2022 The importance of providing early\n\ninformation on crop yields had also been highlighted to facilitate timely decision-making with respect to the impact\u2019s failings and appropriate interventions.\n\n\u2022 Raising farmers\u2019 awareness of drought\n\n-resistant crop varieties and short-duration crops and the need to bring\n\nforward the Yala cultivation season by two weeks and the provision of advance information regarding harvesting has also been discussed.\n\n\u2022 Regarding requirement for guidelines\n\nto be formulated for agriculture and food security, officials from the Ministry of Agriculture have been instructed to take the necessary steps and raise awareness among farmers and officials.\n\n\u2022 During the Committee meeting, discussions were held regarding the likelihood of the occurrence of a Super El Ni\u00f1o event and its potential impacts. It had been noted that forecasting weather conditions during such an event could be challenging and that extreme weather conditions may occur."
  },
