    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "bbf5c78ec6d03e9e6359f0e1fa4ca4a2",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1955,
    "chunk_text": "\u2022 During the Committee meeting, discussions were held regarding the likelihood of the occurrence of a Super El Ni\u00f1o event and its potential impacts. It had been noted that forecasting weather conditions during such an event could be challenging and that extreme weather conditions may occur.\n\n\u2022 The Committee had further discussed the need to implement necessary measures to address potential issues relating to the supply of drinking water and declining water levels in reservoirs.\n\n\u2022 It had been noted that, in managing water resources in districts potentially affected by El Ni\u00f1o conditions, groundwater resources should be properly managed and water levels in reservoirs and tanks should be continuously monitored.\n\n\u2022 It had been further emphasized that accurate, district-level weather forecasts should be provided to relevant institutions to enable them to take timely and precautionary actions.\n\n\u2022 A media briefing on El Ni\u00f1o impacts had been conducted on 20th August, 2026 to raise public awareness regarding the prevailing situation. It had been communicated that the Government is continuously monitoring the situation and will take prompt and appropriate action whenever necessary.\n\n3. Disaster Management Centre\n\nBudget allocations - Details are given in Annex 1.\n\nBudget provisions specifically allocated to the Disaster Management Centre for disaster preparedness and emergency response are managed under the approved annual Government Budget and relevant Treasury provisions.\n\n2065 2066\n\n\u0db4\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dbd\u0dd2\u0db8\u0dda\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd4\u0dc0\u0dd4\u0dc0\n\nNational Disaster Relief Services Centre\n\nThe following measures have been taken to ensure the provision of drinking water and related relief services to populations affected by drought conditions:\n\nProvision of drinking water\n\nPriority is given to supplying drinking water. Bottled drinking water is provided only in instances where such supply is not feasible.\n\nEligibility for Distribution"
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_hansard_2020s",
    "doc_id": "2026-09-24-2026-09-24",
    "num": "2026-09-24",
    "date_str": "2026-09-24",
    "description": "Hansard of 2026-09-24",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.parliament.lk/en/business-of-parliament/hansards",
    "lang": "si-ta-en",
    "url_pdf": "https://www.parliament.lk/uploads/businessdocs/english/24400_english_2026-09-24.pdf",
    "chunk_id": "2026-09-24-2026-09-24-0078",
    "chunk_index": 78,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "c50be8304b3d47309e8ad3f203bd0815",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1987,
    "chunk_text": "The following measures have been taken to ensure the provision of drinking water and related relief services to populations affected by drought conditions:\n\nProvision of drinking water\n\nPriority is given to supplying drinking water. Bottled drinking water is provided only in instances where such supply is not feasible.\n\nEligibility for Distribution\n\n\u2022 District Secretary\n\n\u2022 Divisional Secretary/Assistant Divisional Secretary - Provision of drinking water during drought conditions (Including El Ni\u00f1o preparedness) by National Disaster Relief Services Centre\n\n\u2022 Representative of the local authority\n\n\u2022 Medical Officer of Health/ Public Health Inspector\n\n\u2022 District and Divisional Development Officers (Disaster Relief Services) and\n\n\u2022 Grama Niladari\n\nDistribution of water is undertaken only in areas where,\n\n\u2022 all existing water sources are dry or insufficient;\n\n\u2022 no portable water source is available within a 750-metre radius; and\n\n\u2022 no water supply scheme is available through the National Water Supply and Drainage Board -NWSDB - or other institutions.\n\nEmergency Measures\n\nWhere severe drought conditions are declared by the Department of Meteorology and a large number of people are affected, drinking water is supplied at the Divisional Secretariat level. Coordination and Implementation\n\nDistrict Secretaries coordinate with the National Disaster Relief Services Centre - NDRSC - to ensure effective implementation. Water is sourced only from locations approved by the National Water Supply and Drainage Board - NWSDB - or authorized officers under the Food Act.\n\nApproved Expenditure\n\nThe following expenditures are permitted for water distribution:\n\n\u2022 Fuel costs for water bowsers\n\n\u2022 Overtime allowances for drivers and assistants\n\n\u2022 Payments for temporary drivers and assistants (as per District Price Committee rates)\n\n\u2022 Other essential operational expenses (Maintenance and servicing costs of water bowsers are not covered.)\n\nWater Allocation"
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_hansard_2020s",
