    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "551812d515a04a954697a2b9615351ad",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1354,
    "chunk_text": "The Government has been closely monitoring the evolving El Ni\u00f1o and positive IOD conditions, strengthening preparedness measures for possible extreme weather events and utilizes the forecasts issued by the Department of Meteorology for timely planning and risk management.\n\n5. Contingency measures:\n\nThe DMC has activated preparedness coordination mechanisms including dissemination of early warnings, coordination meetings, emergency operation arrangements, district-level preparedness planning, public awareness activities and inter-agency coordination for anticipated drought and related hazards.\n\n6. Public awareness:\n\nThe DMC conducts public awareness and preparedness programmes through District Disaster Management Coordinating Units, media briefings, community-based disaster risk reduction programmes and dissemination of early warning information in collaboration with relevant agencies. As of now, 10 districts have been affected, including 31 Divisional Secretaries' Divisions.\n\nDetails are given in Annexes 2-1 and 3.\n\n7. International assistance: The DMC coordinates with international development and humanitarian partners for disaster risk reduction, preparedness, capacity development and emergency response support, whenever required. Details of funding arrangements with development partners are maintained by the respective agencies."
  },
