    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "a975cdbcf8ed31618a16b0ac523783d9",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1719,
    "chunk_text": "7. International assistance: The DMC coordinates with international development and humanitarian partners for disaster risk reduction, preparedness, capacity development and emergency response support, whenever required. Details of funding arrangements with development partners are maintained by the respective agencies.\n\nProviding Relief According to Circular 01/2020: Accordingly, the provision of immediate relief and compensation for loss of life and property damages resulting from natural disasters, as specified in Paragraph 04 of Circular No. 1/2020, was implemented with effect from April 1, 2020, utilizing allocations from the General Treasury. Necessary steps were taken by the Divisional Secretaries and the District Secretaries in coordination with the Disaster Management Division, the National Disaster Relief Services Centre and the District Disaster Management Units under the purview of the Ministry in charge of disaster management to ensure emergency response, deliver prompt relief to disaster-affected individuals and grant compensation for affected persons and damaged properties.\n\nEnhancing Relief During the \u201cDitwah\u201d Disaster Situation: However, during the \u201cDitwah\u201d disaster situation, the Government provided a higher extent of relief including allowances and compensation for the affected public compared to the assistance previously granted under the former insurance scheme.\n\nCurrent Progress in Establishing a New Insurance Scheme (2026):\n\nFurthermore, the following matters were deliberated during the 17th Session of the National Council for Disaster Management held on the 30th June, 2026 under the Chairmanship of His\n\n2069 2070\n\n\u0db4\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dbd\u0dd2\u0db8\u0dda\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd4\u0dc0\u0dd4\u0dc0"
  },
