    "url_pdf": "https://www.parliament.lk/uploads/businessdocs/english/24400_english_2026-09-24.pdf",
    "chunk_id": "2026-09-24-2026-09-24-0083",
    "chunk_index": 83,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "d19509f2f8e558796b5b5d16a692406d",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1747,
    "chunk_text": "Furthermore, the following matters were deliberated during the 17th Session of the National Council for Disaster Management held on the 30th June, 2026 under the Chairmanship of His\n\n2069 2070\n\n\u0db4\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca\u0dbd\u0dd2\u0db8\u0dda\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd4\u0dc0\u0dd4\u0dc0\n\n9. Quantification of losses: The relevant, responsible Ministries coordinate with regard to disaster impact information received from the District Secretariats and the relevant agencies. Further, the Government undertakes to assess post-disaster needs according to the gravity of the disasters, aligning with international loss and damage standards like the International Mechanism for Loss and Damage (WIM). However, estimates relating to agricultural losses, GDP impacts, revenue losses and sectoral economic assessments are produced by the respective Line Ministries and competent authorities. Those, too, have been very carefully evaluated and quantified in sector or area wise. Hon. Member, I table* Annexes 1, 2, 2-1 and 3 for your reference. Thank you, Sir. \u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0dbb\u0dc0\u0dd3 \u0d9a\u0dbb\u0dd4\u0dab\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dba\u0d9a \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0bb0\u0bb5\u0bbf \u0b95\u0bb0\u0bc1\u0ba3\u0bbe\u0ba8\u0bbe\u0baf\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95) (The Hon. Ravi Karunanayake) Hon. Speaker, I must thank the Hon. Deputy Minister for giving a very comprehensive Answer.\n\nHowever, Hon. Deputy Minister, in answer to Question No. 3, you mentioned that there was an allocation of Rs. 12.5 billion under Vote No. 1501, but the allocation was Rs. 4.8 billion. So, it is a matter that you should look into.\n\nThen, there was a news report in the \"Daily Mirror\" titled \"El Ni\u00f1o: NWSDB has only 100 water bowsers\". So, since you say that the per capita water consumption had been increased from six litres to 15 litres, there would be a delivery problem."
  },
