    "description": "Hansard of 2026-09-24",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.parliament.lk/en/business-of-parliament/hansards",
    "lang": "si-ta-en",
    "url_pdf": "https://www.parliament.lk/uploads/businessdocs/english/24400_english_2026-09-24.pdf",
    "chunk_id": "2026-09-24-2026-09-24-0124",
    "chunk_index": 124,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "a424c094890f0c22cd268c2dcefc9c95",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1549,
    "chunk_text": "With this Amendment, we are able to, as required, establish Appeal Courts in the provinces. There are various interpretations being brought about with regard to these Amendments we have initiated or what is being made possible, but the fact of the matter is that each of these Amendments and each of these initiatives made through this are an attempt to make justice more accessible to all without discrimination.\n\n2091 2092\n\n2026 \u0dc3\u0dd0\u0db4\u0dca\u0dad\u0dd0\u0db8\u0dca\u0db6\u0dbb\u0dca 24\n\nIt is important, Sir, to understand the true impact of what happens when justice is delayed and who actually benefits when justice is delayed. Though everyday citizens or the normal people in this country experience these delays in ways which fundamentally make their lives unbearable, we know that the delays in the justice system have benefited an elite in this country as well. Generally, what has been the trend? One Government comes into power and starts investigations, which happen in a very lackadaisical manner and not systematically because everyone is part of the whole system and everyone knows that those are merely rhetorical flourishes and none of the investigations ever lead to anything meaningful. Then, that Government changes and a new Government comes into power, and the cases are either withheld or dismissed, and the cycle continues. No one with power or from a political background was ever meaningfully held accountable in this country until these last two years. So, it is only now that we see justice really being applied to all without discrimination."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_hansard_2020s",
