    "chunk_index": 154,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "ccc4f4a50c261b978117cb7ececd5926",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1753,
    "chunk_text": "The current Government enjoys a comfortable two-thirds majority in this House and can easily steamroll its way through Parliament. But, that is precisely what our Government, under the leadership of President Anura Kumara Dissanayake, has sought to avoid, Sir.\n\nWe have a mandate for system change. We are on track, and that is why many people, including some in the legal profession who, unfortunately, benefited from a corrupt system, are resisting the reforms right now.\n\n\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0db1\u0dd2\u0dba\u0ddd\u0da2\u0dca\u200d\u0dba\u0dba \u0d9a\u0dae\u0dcf\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dba\u0d9a\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dcf\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0baa\u0bbf\u0bb0\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0b9a\u0bcd \u0b9a\u0baa\u0bbe\u0ba8\u0bbe\u0baf\u0b95\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0b85\u0bb5\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd) (The Hon. Deputy Speaker) Hon. (Ms.) Lakmali Hemachandra, you have two minutes left of your original time. However, you may avail yourself of further time, as per the request of the Chief Government Whip.\n\n\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0db1\u0dd3\u0dad\u0dd2\u0da5 \u0dbd\u0d9a\u0dca\u0db8\u0dcf\u0dbd\u0dd2 \u0dc4\u0dda\u0db8\u0da0\u0db1\u0dca\u0daf\u0dca\u200d\u0dbb\u0dbb \u0db8\u0dd9\u0db1\u0dd9\u0dc0\u0dd2\u0dba\u0dc0\u0dd2\u0dba (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0b9a\u0b9f\u0bcd\u0b9f\u0ba4\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0bb0\u0ba3\u0bbf (\u0b9a\u0bc6\u0bb2\u0bcd\u0bb5\u0bbf) \u0bb2\u0b95\u0bcd\u0bae\u0bbe\u0bb2\u0bbf \u0bb9\u0bc7\u0bae\u0b9a\u0ba8\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0bb0)\u0bae\u0b9a\u0ba8\u0bcd\u0ba4\u0bbf\u0bb0) (The Hon. (Ms.) Lakmali Hemachandra, Attorney-at-Law) Thank you, Sir.\n\nConsider what happened in 2015, for example, when the \"Yahapalana\" Government came into power and reinstated Shirani Bandaranayake. The then Chief Justice Mohan Peiris reportedly pleaded with President Maithreepala Sirisena to allow him to remain as Chief Justice. He was alleged to have offered to deliver rulings in whatever way the new Government wanted in exchange for retaining his position. However, Sir, thanks to the people of this country and especially, to this Government, that era is over. We are firmly on the road to reform and recovery."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_hansard_2020s",
    "doc_id": "2026-09-24-2026-09-24",
    "num": "2026-09-24",
    "date_str": "2026-09-24",
    "description": "Hansard of 2026-09-24",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.parliament.lk/en/business-of-parliament/hansards",
    "lang": "si-ta-en",
    "url_pdf": "https://www.parliament.lk/uploads/businessdocs/english/24400_english_2026-09-24.pdf",
    "chunk_id": "2026-09-24-2026-09-24-0155",
    "chunk_index": 155,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "ab50dd01f0975573319a7afb76dfd13f",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1188,
    "chunk_text": "Consider what happened in 2015, for example, when the \"Yahapalana\" Government came into power and reinstated Shirani Bandaranayake. The then Chief Justice Mohan Peiris reportedly pleaded with President Maithreepala Sirisena to allow him to remain as Chief Justice. He was alleged to have offered to deliver rulings in whatever way the new Government wanted in exchange for retaining his position. However, Sir, thanks to the people of this country and especially, to this Government, that era is over. We are firmly on the road to reform and recovery.\n\nAlso, there is a fundamental difference between reducing judges' tenure and increasing the retirement age uniformly. A reduction threatens the security of tenure. It tells judges that Parliament or the Executive can shorten their service. A reduction definitely threatens the independence of the Judiciary. A general increase does not remove a judge from office or make the continued service dependent on pleasing the Government. This is a general extension awarded to all judges. Therefore, Sir, their work in the future is not dependent on pleasing the Government or the Executive. That is the reality of the Twenty Second Amendment."
  },
  {
