    "chunk_text": "And, finally, if I may say, obviously, our system, again is going by the letter of the law. Our system states that we have to go to the Supreme Court and the Supreme Court can rule on whatever laws that Parliament chooses to debate and pass. But, on this particular matter, there is\n\nFinally, Sir, let me conclude by just saying this. There are so many other important day-to-day matters that concern people. But, this Government chooses to act in a manner that is completely unacceptable. There is one example I want to give and I think some of my Colleagues representing the North and the East have already spoken about it. As you know, this week commemorates Thileepan, a former cadre of the LTTE who fasted unto death and sacrificed his life on a 26th of September, which arrives in a couple of days\u2019 time. That event has been held despite there had been several oppositions in the past where governments, particularly the Rajapaksa Government, had tried to disrupt it. Nonetheless, the people held these events. Last year, your Members from Jaffna attended those events. They attended those events, garlanded statues of Thiyaga Theepam Thileepan. The Hon. Minister Chandrasekar also attended the event; he wanted to go in, but there was opposition to his taking part in it. But, this time, whilst the event was taking place very peacefuliy with a lot of participation, all of a sudden, the police went there and removed all the speakers. Then, they had said that there is a threat to national security and that without the intelligence reports, they would not able to hand over the speakers again. Sir, we talk about police and we talk about all of this.\n\n\u0db8\u0dd6\u0dbd\u0dcf\u0dc3\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dd6\u0daa \u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0db8\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dca\u200d\u0dbb\u0dd3\u0dd3\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dcf\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0ba4\u0bb2\u0bc8\u0bae\u0bc8\u0ba4\u0bbe\u0b99\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bcd \u0b89\u0bb1\u0bc1\u0baa\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bbf\u0ba9\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0b85\u0bb5\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd)\u0ba4\u0bbe\u0b99\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bcd \u0b89\u0bb1\u0bc1\u0baa\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bbf\u0ba9\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0b85\u0bb5\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd) (The Hon. Presiding Member) \u0dad\u0dc0\u0dad\u0dca \u0d9a\u0dcf\u0dbd\u0dba \u0dbd\u0db6\u0dcf \u0daf\u0dd3\u0db8\u0da7 \u0db1\u0ddc\u0dc4\u0dd0\u0d9a\u0dd2\u0dba\u0dd2, \u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0db8\u0db1\u0dca\u0dad\u0dca\u200d\u0dbb\u0dd3\u0dd3\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0db1\u0dd2.\u0dd4\u0db8\u0db1\u0dd2.\n\n\u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0da2\u0dd3.\u0da2\u0dd3. \u0db4\u0ddc\u0db1\u0dca\u0db1\u0db8\u0dca\u0db6\u0dbd\u0db8\u0dca \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0b9c\u0bc0.\u0b9c\u0bc0. \u0baa\u0bca\u0ba9\u0bcd\u0ba9\u0bae\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bb2\u0bae\u0bcd) \u0ba9\u0bcd\u0ba9\u0bae\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bb2\u0bae\u0bcd) (The Hon. G.G. Ponnambalam) I am concluding, Sir."
